struct iphdr *iph = skb->encapsulation ? inner_ip_hdr(skb) : ip_hdr(skb);
if (!(iph->frag_off & htons(IP_DF)))
Reason:
Directly dereferencing `ip_hdr()` or `inner_ip_hdr()` is unsafe for packets from PF_PACKET paths because the skb header may not be linear, causing reads of uninitialized memory and triggering a KMSAN warning.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
const struct iphdr *iph;
struct iphdr _iph;
int nhoff = skb->encapsulation ? skb_inner_network_offset(skb) : skb_network_offset(skb);
iph = skb_header_pointer(skb, nhoff, sizeof(_iph), &_iph);
if (!iph || !(iph->frag_off & htons(IP_DF)))
Reason:
`skb_header_pointer()` safely reads the IPv4 header, handling both linear and non-linear skb data. The subsequent null check ensures robustness if the pointer is invalid.

